ailure after obtaining the refusal binding, verify the source tenant, pending decision, conversation and protected transcript remain unchanged, then restore storage and demonstrate one successful resolution with the intended history outcome.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"evidence_gaps\": [\n    \"E1 — crates/desktop-core/tests/harness_tools/main.rs covers stale resolutions, successful guarded switching/setup completion and history-removal failures, but does not inject failure of the tenant-state save during resolution. The retained passing suites and native runs therefore do not establish R1's refusal/recovery behavior. Add and retain the production-interface regressions specified in R1.\"\n  ],\n  \"optional_suggestions\": [\n    \"apps/desktop/src/v2/inbox/inbox.tsx:177: allow filter-tab height to accommodate wrapping at 200% zoom. The current inbox-900x600-200-light.png capture still shows counts extending below the fixed-height tab backgrounds.\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Reproduced all four supplied fingerprints. All 4,040 scoped hashes and 18,338 compiled-input entries matched, including final rechecks. Independently enumerated inventory membership found no missing or additional paths; all 18 check-log hashes matched. These checks establish consistency, not compiler execution or evidence authorship. The compiled-input procedure excludes target and node_modules.\",\n    \"Verified C29 attempt-09's receipt, matching passing raw verdict, request binding and unchanged scoped files. C28 and C27 receipt-to-verdict bindings also matched. D058/D059 permit the integration while C26 remains open; no controller, phase or release completion is inferred.\",\n    \"The prior stale-resolution defect is addressed by native refusal references bound to source context, destination, pending conversation/decision and setup generation, together with renderer retry retirement. R1 above concerns the separate persistence-failure path.\",\n    \"Accept the documented metho