{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/shell.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/inbox-reads.md; rg -n 'R2Inbox|Fresh|C30|V2-(R01|R02|R04|R08|R09|T01|T02|T04|T12|T13)' docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md docs/planning/test-catalogue.md docs/architecture/checks.json docs/architecture/native-checks.json; sed -n '2446,2515p' docs/planning/decisions.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Shell, Home, tenant switcher, palette, toasts\n\nSource: `prototype/R2App.dc.html` (sidebar markup, `nav`, `switchPatch`,\n`requestSwitch`, `palette*`, `toast*`, `top`, Home section). Chunk: C28 (shell,\nHome skeleton), C30 (Home attention list backed by Inbox scope).\n\n## Sidebar\n\n- Top: tenant switcher button showing tenant name and environment pill;\n  ⌘T opens the list. Entries: every tenant (name, environment, TSG), then\n  \"Add a tenant…\". Selected tenant uses `sel/selInk`.\n- Destinations in the order of DESIGN-V2 §5 with icon, label, shortcut hint.\n  Unavailable destinations render disabled with their availability reason as\n  a tooltip and accessible description, never hidden.\n- Bottom: appearance toggle (light/dark/system) and \"Show the calls\" toggle,\n  both dispatching their Rust preference.\n- Collapses to icons below 1280px window width.\n\n## Home\n\n- Title \"Home\" with the tenant name and environment beneath; last-read line\n  from `ReadStatus` (\"Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete\" or\n  \"· 3 sources partial\", warn-styled when partial; \"First read pending\" on a\n  fresh tenant).\n- \"Needs attention\": up to five Inbox items of kind Needs action, each with\n  severity (colour + icon + word), title, product, action button that\n  navigates with context, Acknowledge, and Snooze whose tooltip and\n  accessible name are the item's `snoozeLabel`.\n- Product cards for admitted, licensed products with their read state;\n  unlicensed products are listed once as \"Not licensed in this tenant\" and\n  unavailable products once as \"Not available in this release\" (DESIGN-V2\n  §6), never hidden.\n- Playground card (Runtime Security scan): prompt, direction, profile select,\n  verdict panel (word + icon + reason + plain explanation). Verdicts are\n  profile-aware: a detector not enabled, or a topic not assigned, reads \"Not\n  detected\" with the reason; monitor-only turns Blocked into Flagged with the\n  profile named.\n\n## Tenant switch (I1, I2)\n\n- `switchTenant{tenant_id, resolution?}`; the core refuses with\n  `SwitchBlocked{pending: {conversation, decision}}` when a Harness decision is\n  pending. The UI renders the guard dialog (Archive and switch / Discard and\n  switch / Stay) from that payload and re-dispatches with `resolution`. Initial\n  focus is on Stay, the safe default (Enter on arrival never ends the\n  conversation); Archive and switch stays the visually primary action.\n- Every entry point (switcher, palette, menu, wizard completion) uses the same\n  intent. After a switch the new tenant's Home renders from cached scopes within\n  100 ms with read status pending until the read lands.\n\n## Command palette\n\n- ⌘K. Entries: destinations from the Rust inventory, tenants, and three actions\n  (Navigate, Switch tenant, Read now). Typing filters; Enter dispatches; Escape\n  closes and restores focus. Native menu navigation while the palette is open\n  closes it first.\n\n## Toasts (I10)\n\n- Kinds ok, info, warn with icon and colour; one visible at a time, newest\n  replaces; 6 s expiry (persist under Reduce Motion); optional Undo action\n  (snooze). A toast never carries information absent from an observed scope.\n\n## Modals (I8)\n\n- Stack order kept in the shell store; only the topmost is interactive;\n  siblings get `aria-hidden`; Escape closes the topmost; focus returns to the\n  opener. Detail sheets (transcripts, facts) are modals in this stack.\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Fixture boards: R2Palette, R2Tenants, R2Dark, R2App default.\n- V2-T01, T02, T09, T10, T11; V2-N01, N03, N04, N05.\n# Inbox and reads\n\nSource: `R2App` (`ITEMS`, `visibleItems`, `ack`, `snoozed`, `snooze`,\n`inboxRows`, `sel`, `startRead`, `recheck`, `toGo`). Chunk: C30.\n\n## Inbox\n\n- Tabs All / Needs action / Updates / Snoozed with counts. Rows: severity\n  (colour + icon + word), title, product, source line (\"API keys · cached\",\n  \"rotated 07:46\"), when, acknowledged mark. Selecting opens the detail pane:\n  body, facts table, \"Why this matters\" explanation, action button (navigates\n  with context), Acknowledge / Mark as needing action, Snooze or Unsnooze.\n- Empty states distinguish \"first read pending\" from \"nothing needs action\"\n  and name partial sources (\"3 of 6 sources were read at 07:45\").\n- Snooze: per item, core-computed return time, 24 hours for every item in\n  P09 (the prototype's deadline-bound rotation snooze is not carried: no\n  admitted operation has a grace deadline, P20). The label, toast and\n  Snoozed-tab \"Returns …\" text all state the same time (I11). The\n  `deadline` field stays optional for a future item that has a real one.\n- Contextual navigation: an item's action carries a target (screen, product,\n  tab, conversation). Into an ended conversation it sets a transient hint\n  offering \"Open the saved transcript\" and \"Start a new investigation\".\n\n## Reads (I4)\n\n- `readTenant` runs a finite read of every selected product; `ReadStatus`\n  carries per-product state (pending, ok, partial, needsRole), last-read\n  time and counts. First read on a fresh tenant shows pending everywhere.\n- Completion toast: ok \"Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete\" or\n  warn \"· 3 sources partial\"; for fresh tenants \"· 1 product still needs a\n  role\" or \"· no activity yet in <tenant>\". `recheckProduct` after a role is\n  granted shows an info toast and re-reads.\n\n## Core contract\n\n- Scope `InboxItem{id, kind, severity, title, product, source, when, body,\n  facts, action_target, explanation, deadline?, snooze_return?, acknowledged}`\n  per tenant; intents `acknowledgeItem`, `snoozeItem`, `unsnoozeItem`,\n  `readTenant`, `recheckProduct`.\n- The rotation reminder (`rotation-<application>`) is a distinct item id from\n  the expiry alert and clears only when the old key's deletion is read back\n  (I7). Items exist only for admitted products (DESIGN-V2 §6).\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Board R2Inbox. Tests V2-R02, R04, R08, R09; V2-T04, T12, T13; V2-N02.\ndocs/architecture/native-checks.json:1192:    \"C30\": [\ndocs/architecture/native-checks.json:1194:        \"id\": \"C30-N01\",\ndocs/architecture/native-checks.json:1198:        \"id\": \"C30-N02\",\ndocs/architecture/native-checks.json:1202:        \"id\": \"C30-N03\",\ndocs/architecture/native-checks.json:1206:        \"id\": \"C30-N04\",\ndocs/architecture/native-checks.json:1295:        \"check\": \"The Inbox as the prototype draws it (R2App start=inbox) with a tenant whose read has landed: the heading and its line naming the tenant; a 430px list card with the filter tabs (All, Needs action, Updates, Snoozed, each with its count) over the rows (severity tile and word, title, product and source, when; an acknowledged row marked) and a footer naming the read's coverage; selecting a row fills the detail card (severity tile and word, product and source, the 22px title, the body, the facts as a three-column grid, the entry's own action, Acknowledge or Mark as needing action, Snooze or Unsnooze); the empty states name the read (first read pending; the failed first read, every source answering 500; with the sessions chart denied, AI Runtime Security needing a role: Open role issue offered, the footer's partial coverage, the empty pane qualifying what was read and naming the unread source rather than a bare all-clear, and the issue opening that product in Administration); snooze, acknowledge and unsnooze stay the C30 core intents with the core's return time stated the same in the row, the detail and the toast (D059 parity: the composites under evidence/C37/parity are captured by this script from the populated state with the first row opened, parity/bundle.json rewritten with the bundle they came from, and the owner's approval of them is recorded in parity/notes.md).\"\ndocs/architecture/native-checks.json:1313:        \"check\": \"The tenant-switch guard (invariant I1) on the board with a Harness decision waiting: choosing the other tenant from the switcher, from the palette's Switch to entry and from Go \\u203a Switch Tenant\\u2026 each shows the one guard dialog (Stay, Discard and switch, Archive and switch; naming the target tenant; focus on Stay); Escape and Stay keep the first tenant and the waiting decision; Archive and switch ends the conversation with the decision untaken, lands the other tenant on Home and leaves no engine, with nothing further run (C30-N01 carried onto the C38 board in C44).\"\ndocs/architecture/checks.json:2485:    \"C30\": {\ndocs/architecture/checks.json:2507:        \"C30\",\ndocs/architecture/checks.json:3478:      \"C30\",\ndocs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md:15:| R2Tenants | R2App | start=home, overlay=tenants | `fx.switcher` | V2-T01, T02 | C28/C30 |\ndocs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md:29:| R2Inbox | R2App | start=inbox | `fx.inbox` | V2-T04, T12, T13 | C30 |\ndocs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md:30:| R2Fresh | R2App | start=home, tenant never read | `fx.fresh` | first read pending, empty Inbox (I12) | C30 |\n   redacted wire data; English only in P09; chunks commit on main except C34.\n9. C27 proceeds in parallel with C26 (docs and controller registration only);\n   C28 waits for C26.\n\n\n## D059 — P09 re-cut: port the prototype, one gate per screen at 8\n\nAccepted by the owner on 2026-10-29 after a grilling session (23 questions, all\naccepted; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md`). C32 had taken twenty review rounds\nwhile the built v2 screens never matched the design: chunks had wrapped the\nlegacy feature components in v2 frames instead of porting the prototype.\n\n- The frozen prototype (D058, version 134) is the specification per screen; the\n  canvas is not consulted (it is unreachable from the implementing account).\n- A screen is done when it matches its board side by side at 1440×900 in both\n  themes with real core data, judged by the owner from composites kept under\n  the chunk's evidence; parity is structural (regions, widths, spacing, type\n  scale, tokens, component shapes), content differs, accessibility\n  corrections may deviate and are noted. Parity precedes review.\n- One heavy gate per chunk after that approval (rebuild, native acceptance,\n  the full fixture suite, the Codex review), accepted at 8 under D032/D034; the\n  phase review stays 9 and every chunk accepted at 8 is raised in C44.\n- v2 screens import no legacy feature view; the legacy files stay for the\n  legacy shell until C44 removes it. C33 was committed without a receipt (its\n  core stands; its two screens are superseded).\n- Chunks: C35 shell, C36 Home, C37 Inbox fix-up, C38 Harness, C39 Administration\n  (a: Runtime Security, b: other products), C40 Test Cases, C41 API Client,\n  C42 Academy (prototype chrome around the hosted embed), C43 Wizard re-port\n  over the existing state machine, C44 legacy removal on a branch and the P09\n  review. C34 is superseded. `Subject::LAST_CHUNK` is 44.\n\n## Directions explicitly requested before round 1\n\n- Fresh application implementation; the existing GPUI codebase is primarily a\n  reference point.\n- React presentation, Rust application implementation, and the new Rust SCM SDK.\n- Tauri was initially acceptable if needed and is now selected by D008.\n- cdot-framework informs the backend foundation through D008's selective reuse\n  and architecture direction; individual imports still require evaluation.\n- Plan first, architecture improvement review second, implementation and package\n  qualification after that.\n- Independent numeric review gates for testable chunks; earlier requirement:\n  scores below 9/10 require remediation and another actual review.\n\n## Interview exit and remaining evidence\n\nThe product/process frontier through Q23 is settled; D024/D025 subsequently\nsettle source terms and all four architecture candidates. Continue the requested\narchitecture work from those decisions. The prior extra blanket scope-confirmation\nrequest must not prevent already authorized design/research. G01 still requires\nconcrete interfaces/commands and independent review before implementation.\nExact identity strings, dependency pins, import compatibility, named numeric\nbudgets, and designated live environments require explicit evidence/specification\nat their declared gates. They are not secretly assumed complete or reasons to\nrepeat settled product questions. No application implementation has started.\n\n## D060 — No import from the alpha; this desktop is v1\n\nDecided by the owner on 2026-10-31, in the owner's words: \"i really really really don't want to have an import from v1. in fact, i plan on calling this v1 since the previous was an alpha.\"\n\n- The previous desktop (`/Users/cdot/development/cdot65/prisma-airs-desktop`) is the alpha. Nothing is imported from it: the reviewed import of alpha work (C23: the Import from v1 destination and view, the wizard's \"Used Prisma AIRS Desktop 1?\" box and the tenant step's import link, the first-run import frame) is removed from the one presentation in C44, its native checks C23-N01..N09 are retired without replacement, and the legacy-script map and the C44 cumulative set drop `acceptance_c23.py`.\n- Still to decide the same way, in a follow-up chunk the owner names (proposed C45): the core's alpha-import intents and reader (`import_v1_domain`, the `V1Import*` intents, the host adapters), Settings' file-based \"Import tenant profiles\" and the API Client's \"Import v1 API Client profile\" adoption, which are alpha-import surfaces too; their removal changes contracts and earlier chunks' tests and is not done inside the P09 closure.\n- Naming: this desktop becomes v1 and the previous one the alpha. The rename touches the application identity that lets the two coexist (bundle identifiers, data roots, Keychain namespaces, D001-era identities) and the whole document set; it is its own chunk after P09, not a find-and-replace.\n- The product name shown today stays \"Prisma AIRS Desktop v2\" until that chunk.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '155,226p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/observation_domain.rs; sed -n '330,395p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/observation_domain.rs; sed -n '535,662p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/observation_domain.rs; sed -n '3880,3960p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs; rg -n 'storage|intent|require_operator|principal|Harness' crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs | tail -35\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '155,226p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/observation_domain.rs; sed -n '330,395p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/observation_domain.rs; sed -n '535,662p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/observation_domain.rs; sed -n '3880,3960p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs; rg -n 'storage|intent|require_operator|principal|Harness' crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs | tail -35\"","aggregated_output":"    /// The product a `recheckProduct` asked for, until its read lands.\n    pub(super) rechecking: Option<ProductId>,\n    snoozes: u32,\n    pub(super) last_snooze: Option<SnoozeReceipt>,\n}\n\nimpl OverviewRecord {\n    fn new(tenant: TenantId) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            tenant,\n            read: None,\n            failure: None,\n            failed_at: None,\n            parts: Vec::new(),\n            red_team: None,\n            model_skill: None,\n            red_team_failed: None,\n            model_skill_failed: None,\n            generation: 0,\n            rechecking: None,\n            snoozes: 0,\n            last_snooze: None,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Reading: a part admitted under the tenant's current context is\n    /// still under way.\n    pub(super) fn refreshing(&self, current: Option<&ContextRef>) -> bool {\n        self.parts.iter().any(|c| Some(c) == current)\n    }\n\n    /// A product's read settled: an outcome that established at least one\n    /// source replaces the retained outcome (and clears any failure); one\n    /// that established nothing is kept as the latest failed attempt, the\n    /// retained outcome staying shown as older.\n    fn settle_product(&mut self, product: ProductId, outcome: ProductOutcome) {\n        let (slot, failed) = match product {\n            ProductId::RedTeam => (&mut self.red_team, &mut self.red_team_failed),\n            ProductId::ModelSkill => (&mut self.model_skill, &mut self.model_skill_failed),\n            ProductId::RuntimeSecurity | ProductId::Gateway => return,\n        };\n        if outcome.sources_read > 0 {\n            *slot = Some(outcome);\n            *failed = None;\n        } else {\n            *failed = Some(FailedAttempt {\n                at: outcome.read_at,\n                needs_role: outcome.needs_role,\n                failure: outcome.failure,\n                detail: outcome.detail,\n            });\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// One read part landed under `context`. A current part completes the\n    /// read when no current part is left (one generation); a withdrawn\n    /// (retired-context) part counts nothing, and a recheck it carried is\n    /// simply over once nothing current remains.\n    fn part_landed(&mut self, context: &ContextRef, current: Option<&ContextRef>) {\n        if let Some(at) = self.parts.iter().position(|c| c == context) {\n            self.parts.remove(at);\n        }\n        if self.refreshing(current) {\n            return;\n        }\n        if Some(context) == current {\n            self.generation = self.generation.wrapping_add(1);\n        }\n        self.rechecking = None;\n    }\n}\n\n        };\n        &mut self.overviews[at]\n    }\n\n    /// A Home read part was admitted under `context` (the overview, or one\n    /// product's read): the tenant reads until every current part lands.\n    pub(super) fn read_part_started(&mut self, context: &ContextRef) {\n        let Ok(tenant) = self.check_context(context) else {\n            return;\n        };\n        self.record_for(&tenant).parts.push(context.clone());\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn overview_started(&mut self, context: &ContextRef) {\n        self.read_part_started(context);\n    }\n\n    /// A part admitted under a context that has since retired: its reply is\n    /// withdrawn and the tenant stops waiting for it; nothing completed.\n    fn retired_part_done(&mut self, context: &ContextRef) {\n        let current = self.active_ref.clone();\n        if let Some(record) = self\n            .overviews\n            .iter_mut()\n            .find(|r| r.parts.iter().any(|c| c == context))\n        {\n            record.part_landed(context, current.as_ref());\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Records a settled overview read for its context (a retired context's\n    /// read is never kept).\n    pub(super) fn overview_settled(&mut self, context: &ContextRef, result: ManagementResult) {\n        if self.active_ref.as_ref() != Some(context) {\n            self.retired_part_done(context);\n            return;\n        }\n        let Some(tenant) = self.data.active.clone() else {\n            return;\n        };\n        let clock = self.clock();\n        let current = self.active_ref.clone();\n        let record = self.record_for(&tenant);\n        // A completed read of the current context: the presentation may\n        // announce it (C30, I4), and a recheck is answered by it.\n        record.part_landed(context, current.as_ref());\n        match result {\n            // Every source failed: a failed refresh. The last read stays\n            // (marked by the failure); with none, the failed read is shown.\n            ManagementResult::Overview { overview }\n                if overview.chart.is_none()\n                    && overview.keys_failure.is_some()\n                    && overview\n                        .gateway\n                        .as_ref()\n                        .is_none_or(|g| g.usage_failure.is_some() && g.policies.is_none()) =>\n            {\n                record.failure = overview.chart_failure.or(overview.keys_failure);\n                record.failed_at = Some(clock);\n                if record.read.is_none() {\n                    record.read = Some(overview);\n                }\n            }\n            ManagementResult::Overview { overview } => {\n                record.failure = None;\n                record.failed_at = None;\n        let current = self.active_ref.clone();\n        let record = self.record_for(&tenant);\n        record.part_landed(context, current.as_ref());\n        record.settle_product(product, outcome);\n    }\n\n    /// A product's read was asked for but not admitted: a finite, named\n    /// failure rather than a part that never lands.\n    pub(super) fn product_read_refused(\n        &mut self,\n        tenant: &TenantId,\n        product: ProductId,\n        refusal: Refusal,\n    ) {\n        let clock = self.clock();\n        let record = self.record_for(tenant);\n        let outcome = ProductOutcome {\n            read_at: clock,\n            sources_read: 0,\n            sources_total: product_sources(product),\n            missing: all_missing(product),\n            needs_role: false,\n            failure: None,\n            detail: format!(\"The read was not admitted ({refusal:?}).\"),\n        };\n        record.settle_product(product, outcome);\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn set_rechecking(&mut self, tenant: &TenantId, product: Option<ProductId>) {\n        self.record_for(tenant).rechecking = product;\n    }\n\n    /// The items the current read reports, plus the active tenant's setup\n    /// warnings (C29), which holds address like any other item.\n    fn current_items(&self, context: &ContextRef) -> Vec<InboxItem> {\n        let Ok(tenant) = self.check_context(context) else {\n            return Vec::new();\n        };\n        let mut items: Vec<InboxItem> = self\n            .overviews\n            .iter()\n            .find(|r| r.tenant == tenant)\n            .and_then(|r| r.read.as_ref())\n            .map(|r| r.items.clone())\n            .unwrap_or_default();\n        if self.active_ref.as_ref() == Some(context) {\n            items.extend(self.setup_warning_items());\n            items.extend(self.rotation_items());\n        }\n        items\n    }\n\n    /// The active tenant's holds.\n    pub(super) fn active_holds(&self) -> &[Hold] {\n        self.data\n            .active\n            .as_ref()\n            .and_then(|t| self.holds.iter().find(|(h, _)| h == t))\n            .map_or(&[], |(_, h)| h.as_slice())\n    }\n\n    /// Acknowledges or snoozes an attention item the current read reports.\n    pub(super) fn hold_insight(\n        &mut self,\n        context: &ContextRef,\n        id: &str,\n        kind: HoldKind,\n    ) -> Result<(), Refusal> {\n        let tenant = self.check_context(context)?;\n        let item = self\n            .current_items(context)\n            .into_iter()\n            .find(|i| i.id == id)\n            .ok_or(Refusal::InvalidInput)?;\n        let clock = self.clock();\n        let entry = match self.holds.iter().position(|(t, _)| t == &tenant) {\n            Some(i) => &mut self.holds[i].1,\n            None => {\n                self.holds.push((tenant.clone(), Vec::new()));\n                &mut self.holds.last_mut().expect(\"pushed\").1\n            }\n        };\n        entry.retain(|h| h.id != id);\n        if entry.len() >= HOLD_LIMIT {\n            return Err(Refusal::Busy);\n        }\n        let until = clock.saturating_add(SNOOZE_SECS);\n        entry.push(Hold {\n            id: id.to_owned(),\n            kind,\n            level: level(&item),\n            until,\n        });\n        if kind == HoldKind::Snooze {\n            // The receipt the presentation announces once (C30, I11).\n            let record = self.record_for(&tenant);\n            record.snoozes = record.snoozes.wrapping_add(1);\n            record.last_snooze = Some(SnoozeReceipt {\n                id: id.to_owned(),\n                title: item.title,\n                returns_at: until,\n                sequence: record.snoozes,\n            });\n        }\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn restore_insight(\n        &mut self,\n        context: &ContextRef,\n        id: &str,\n    ) -> Result<(), Refusal> {\n        let tenant = self.check_context(context)?;\n        let holds = self\n            .holds\n            .iter_mut()\n            .find(|(t, _)| t == &tenant)\n            .ok_or(Refusal::InvalidInput)?;\n        let before = holds.1.len();\n        holds.1.retain(|h| h.id != id);\n        (holds.1.len() < before)\n            .then_some(())\n            .ok_or(Refusal::InvalidInput)\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn forget_holds(&mut self, tenant: &TenantId) {\n        self.holds.retain(|(t, _)| t != tenant);\n        self.overviews.retain(|r| &r.tenant != tenant);\n                    features::ProductId::RedTeam | features::ProductId::ModelSkill\n                )\n            }) {\n                match state.admit_read_part(\n                    context.clone(),\n                    product,\n                    Arc::clone(&adapters.keychain),\n                    Arc::clone(session),\n                ) {\n                    Ok((_, more)) => starts.extend(more),\n                    Err(refusal) => state.product_read_refused(&tenant, product, refusal),\n                }\n            }\n            state.set_rechecking(&tenant, None);\n            operation_ref = Some(operation);\n            effects.push(Effect::Start(starts));\n            effects.push(Effect::Start(state.take_gateway_starts()));\n            state.changed();\n        }\n        Intent::RecheckProduct { context, product } => {\n            let tenant = state.check_context(&context)?;\n            if !state.selected_products(&tenant).contains(&product) {\n                return Err(Refusal::InvalidInput);\n            }\n            let (operation, starts) = match product {\n                features::ProductId::RuntimeSecurity | features::ProductId::Gateway => state\n                    .admit_management(\n                        context,\n                        ManagementRequest::Overview,\n                        Arc::clone(&adapters.keychain),\n                        Arc::clone(session),\n                    )?,\n                features::ProductId::RedTeam | features::ProductId::ModelSkill => stat