{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/harness.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/academy.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/api-client-test-cases.md; sed -n '1,115p' docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/wizard.md; sed -n '1,95p' docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md; sed -n '160,181p' docs/planning/decisions.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/harness.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/academy.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/api-client-test-cases.md; sed -n '1,115p' docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/wizard.md; sed -n '1,95p' docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md; sed -n '160,181p' docs/planning/decisions.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Harness\n\nSource: `R2App` (`CONVOS` blocks/mcp/keys at lines 760–790, `decs`, `ended`,\n`archiveActive`, `sendDraft`, `startNewConvo`, `convoHint`, `follows`),\nboards R2Harness, R2Harness2, R2Harness3. Chunk: C32.\n\nThe screen is a re-skin of the existing Harness engine, sessions, decisions,\nMCP and sign-in modules (C19–C22); the conversation, decision and project\nauthority model is unchanged. D014's Harness restrictions hold: a proposal\nnever authorises Apply.\n\n## Layout\n\n- Title row \"Harness\" with tenant and engine status; left rail of\n  conversations (lifecycle seeds appear only on non-fresh fixture tenants;\n  user conversations titled from their first message; archived ones marked\n  ended); main transcript; one composer per tenant and workspace (its draft kept across navigation, tenant round trips and a conversation's retirement), with messages that reached no conversation, or whose delivery was not confirmed, kept apart for recovery and never sent by themselves (provenance P50).\n- Prerequisites checklist (tenant, management client, Gateway workspace,\n  company sign-in) stays visible until satisfied (D057 F05).\n\n## Lifecycles (fixture conversations)\n\nAll three are **read-only** tool-call lifecycles in the prototype; none\nwrites to a tenant from the Harness.\n\n1. **blocks** — \"Why were 14 prompts blocked on claims-triage overnight?\":\n   read-only tool call `list_security_events` (in-page Approve once /\n   Decline), result summary, recommendation, follow-up \"Open the review\"\n   that opens the injection-override topic review in Administration\n   (Runtime Security, `ChangeKind::Topics`).\n2. **mcp** — \"Which laptops run an MCP server that is not on the allow\n   list?\": in the prototype the read-only call targets an AES inventory.\n   AES has no admitted service (DESIGN-V2 §6), so the implemented fixture\n   reads the workspace MCP server inventory the core already exposes\n   (`GatewayRead::McpServers`, C22) and its follow-up opens a Gateway\n   guardrail review (`ChangeKind::GatewayGuardrails`). Recorded as\n   deviation P16.\n3. **keys** — \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate\n   them?\": read-only key inventory; the Harness refuses to rotate (\"rotation\n   is a write; it goes through Administration and a review\") and hands off\n   to the key rotation flow. The follow-up text reflects the rotation stage\n   (additional key issued / old key removed).\n\nEach has approve, decline, end and follow-up paths. Declining records the\ndecision and the assistant's declined text; ending seals the session\n(`endConversation` → archive id) and the rail shows it ended.\n\nTool-call approval stays as C21/C22 built it: the core decides from the\ntool's write flag whether the host's native confirmation sheet is required;\nread-only calls use the in-page bar. No P09 fixture exercises a write-capable\ncall; the native sheet path is covered by the existing C21 tests.\n\n## Rules\n\n- A fresh tenant's first send creates a user conversation (I12); sending in\n  an ended conversation creates a new one.\n- Contextual navigation into an ended conversation shows a hint with \"Open\n  the saved transcript\" (archived transcript detail) and \"Start a new\n  investigation\" (new conversation prefilled with the opening question). The\n  hint clears on any navigation.\n- A pending decision blocks tenant switch (I1).\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Boards R2Harness (blocks), R2Harness2 (mcp), R2Harness3 (keys). Tests\n  V2-R01, V2-T01, T13; V2-T17 approve/decline/end/follow-up per lifecycle;\n  V2-T18 the keys lifecycle never dispatches a mutation from the Harness.\n# Academy embed\n\nSource: `R2App` Academy section, board R2Academy. Chunk: C34.\n\nThe Academy learner view (react-query, react-router, Academy ShellFrame) is\nhosted inside the new shell unchanged: the new sidebar replaces its outer\nframe, its inner routing and tests stay intact. Gamification appears only\nhere. The wizard's Academy step is the only other Academy surface.\n\nTokens: Academy's `--academy-*` variables remain its own; within the embed\nscope the shell aliases nothing. The embed receives the Rust-owned theme.\n\nTests: existing Academy presentation tests unchanged; one shell test that the\nembed mounts under `academy` and receives theme changes.\n# API Client and Test Cases\n\nSource: `R2App` (`REQ`, `hist`, `send`, `rawJson`, `CASES`, `packCases`,\n`caseRows` lines 1033–1037, `runScan`). Chunk: C33. Both are re-skins of the\nexisting workbench (C14–C15) and library (C12) modules to the layout rhythm.\nNo new remote capability is introduced.\n\n## API Client\n\n- Title row, request tabs (named requests per product), method/URL line with\n  the `get` colour, Send (32px), response pane with status, duration and\n  body; history list of immutable snapshots (I5) from the existing workbench\n  history.\n- After Send, a compact `role=\"status\"` region announces \"<request> · <code>\n  · <duration>\"; the JSON body is outside the live region.\n- Generic requests never bypass AIRS mutation authority (existing C15 rule):\n  a request that would change configuration is refused by the core as today.\n- The \"Show the calls\" panel reuses this response renderer.\n\n## Test Cases\n\n- Title row, filter by product, search, paged table (name, product, input,\n  last result as verdict colour + icon + word), pack-sourced cases carry\n  their pack name.\n- **Runtime-only execution boundary** (prototype lines 1035–1037, parity\n  matrix). A Runtime Security case offers \"Open in Playground\": it sets the\n  Playground's prompt, direction and profile and the operator runs the scan\n  there; the result is stored for the case as a local Playground run. A case\n  for any other product offers \"Inspect\" only: it opens the specification\n  and the recorded result, states which product runs it, and never\n  dispatches a scan or claims execution. Red Team cases say \"hand the spec\n  to a scan\"; no scan is started from this screen.\n- Starter-pack cases selected in the wizard are written at onboarding\n  completion as library entries with `Not run` results.\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Boards R2Api, R2Cases. Tests V2-R05, V2-T05; V2-T14 status region updates\n  after Send with the body outside the live region; V2-T15 non-Runtime rows\n  render Inspect, never Open in Playground, and clicking Inspect dispatches\n  no scan intent (asserted on the mock runtime); V2-T16 paging and filter.\n# First-run wizard and add-tenant sheet\n\nSource: `prototype/R2Onboard.dc.html` (steps, `ERR`, `touch`, `vsig`,\n`verify`, `opened`, `railCtx`, `mode=\"add\"`), `R2App` `addtenant` overlay.\nChunk: C29. Realises D013 (scan-key-first onboarding).\n\n## Steps (first run)\n\n1. **Welcome** — explains that the app is built entirely on Palo Alto\n   Networks' public APIs and exists to show application builders what those\n   interfaces make possible; three cards: Built on the public APIs / See the\n   calls as you go / Learn by doing. Continue.\n2. **Tenant** — name, environment (select), region (select), TSG id, then\n   three credential sections in this order (D013, deviation P17):\n   **Scan key** (required on first run): \"Add scan key…\" opens the host\n   secret sheet and returns a vault id shown as a masked indicator.\n   **Management client** (optional): client id field plus \"Add client\n   secret…\" (host secret sheet); without it Administration is read-only and\n   says so. **Gateway** (optional toggle): workspace name, endpoint URL,\n   \"Add workspace key…\". Secondary action \"Import from Prisma AIRS Desktop\n   v1\" fills name/environment/TSG from the import intent; secrets are always\n   re-entered. Validation per field on blur with\n   `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`; the Continue button names what is\n   missing. After this step the rail shows \"Name · Environment · TSG …\" under\n   its title.\n3. **Products** — cards for the products in DESIGN-V2 §6. Admitted products\n   show licence state read from the tenant and are selectable; Red Team and\n   Model/skill are marked read-only; Agentic Identity Security and Agentic\n   Endpoint Security are shown as \"Not available in this release\" and cannot\n   be selected (P18).\n4. **Verify** — dispatch `verifyTenantSetup`; per-product rows fill as\n   `VerifyStep` results stream (pass / warning / fail with reason) using the\n   existing reads for each admitted product (scan capability check, a\n   management read when a client is present, Gateway prerequisites).\n   Unavailable products show \"Not available\", never a result. The warning\n   and failed rows are fixtures on admitted products. Fail offers \"Fix and verify\n   again\" (returns to Tenant) or \"Continue with warnings\"; warnings become\n   Inbox items on completion.\n5. **Starter packs** (optional) — test-case packs per selected product with\n   counts.\n6. **Academy account** (optional) — sign in or skip; the trust copy states\n   exactly what syncs (Academy progress only).\n7. **Done** — summary; \"Open Prisma AIRS\" is finite (`opening` → done) and\n   dispatches `completeOnboarding`.\n\n## Add-tenant sheet (`mode=\"add\"`)\n\n- 1160×780 sheet over the shell, rail 244px, no Welcome or Academy steps,\n  Cancel at every step; completion dispatches `addTenant` then `switchTenant`.\n  Cancel discards everything except a credential already written by the\n  secret sheet, which is shown in Administration as unattached and can be\n  removed there.\n\n## Core contract\n\n- `verifyTenantSetup{draft}` → stream of `VerifyStep{product, state, reason}`\n  then `VerifyDone{warnings}`.\n- `completeOnboarding{name, env, region, tsg, scan_credential_id,\n  management: {client_id, credential_id}?, gateway: {ws, endpoint,\n  credential_id}?, products, packs, academy_opt_in, warnings}` writes the tenant profile, product\n  selection, packs and Inbox warning items; sets `onboarding=done`.\n- `addTenant{...same minus academy}`.\n- The core never receives a secret through these intents; `credential_ids`\n  reference vault records created by the host secret sheet.\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Boards: see [boards.md](boards.md) (`fx.on.*`, `fx.addTenant`).\n- Tests: step validation and invalidation signature; streaming verify order;\n  cancel semantics; `onboarding` transitions; V2-N02.\n- Live (C29 only): verify against Vulture, reads only, under the designated\n  scope.\n# Prototype boards → test fixtures\n\nEvery wrapper board on the canvas page \"Refined Native v2\" (version 134) is\na reviewed state. Each becomes a named Vitest fixture with the same initial\nprops, so reviewed-state coverage is auditable from this table without the\ncanvas. Props are the `data-props` of `prototype/R2App.dc.html`\n(`start`, `convo`, `theme`, `overlay`) and `prototype/R2Onboard.dc.html`\n(`step`, `filled`, `verify`, `theme`, `mode`).\n\n| Board | Component | Initial props | Fixture id | Primary tests | Chunk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R2App (default) | R2App | start=home, theme=light | `fx.home` | V2-T09, T10, T11 | C28 |\n| R2Dark | R2App | start=home, theme=dark | `fx.home.dark` | token contrast snapshot | C28 |\n| R2Palette | R2App | start=home, overlay=palette | `fx.palette` | palette filter/dispatch, N03 | C28 |\n| R2Tenants | R2App | start=home, overlay=tenants | `fx.switcher` | V2-T01, T02 | C28/C30 |\n| R2AddTenant | R2Onboard | mode=add, step=tenant | `fx.addTenant` | cancel semantics, no Back on the first step | C29 |\n| R2AddTenant drafted | R2Onboard | mode=add, step=tenant, drafted | `fx.addTenant.drafted` | optional scan key, Continue open | C29 |\n| R2On01 Welcome | R2Onboard | step=welcome | `fx.on.welcome` | copy constants | C29 |\n| R2On02 Tenant | R2Onboard | step=tenant, filled=false | `fx.on.tenant.empty` | validation, aria-invalid | C29 |\n| R2On02b Tenant filled | R2Onboard | step=tenant, filled=true | `fx.on.tenant.filled` | rail context line, continue enabled | C29 |\n| R2On03 Products | R2Onboard | step=products | `fx.on.products` | unavailable products not selectable (P18) | C29 |\n| R2On04 Verify | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=running | `fx.on.verify.running` | streaming order | C29 |\n| R2On04b Verify warning | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=warn | `fx.on.verify.warn` | warning row → Inbox item at completion | C29 |\n| R2On04c Verify fail | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=fail | `fx.on.verify.fail` | fix-and-verify-again path | C29 |\n| R2On04d Verify stale | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=done, inputs changed | `fx.on.verify.stale` | results no longer count; later steps unreachable | C29 |\n| R2On05 Packs | R2Onboard | step=packs | `fx.on.packs` | pack counts, optional | C29 |\n| R2On06 Academy | R2Onboard | step=academy | `fx.on.academy` | hosted sign-in or skip (P19) | C29 |\n| R2On07 Done | R2Onboard | step=done | `fx.on.done` | finite open, `onboarding=done` | C29 |\n| R2Inbox | R2App | start=inbox | `fx.inbox` | V2-T04, T12, T13 | C30 |\n| R2Fresh | R2App | start=home, tenant never read | `fx.fresh` | first read pending, empty Inbox (I12) | C30 |\n| R2Admin | R2App | start=admin | `fxAdmin` (v2/admin/administration.test.tsx) | V2-T19, T20, per-tab labels | C31 |\n| R2Review | R2App | start=admin, overlay=review | `fxAdmin` + `review()`/`rotation()` (same file) | V2-T03, T06, T08; T07 in `ui_v2_reviews` | C31 |\n| R2Harness | R2App | start=harness, convo=blocks | `fxHarness` + `harness-lifecycle-blocks.json` (v2/harness/harness.test.tsx) | V2-T17 | C32 |\n| R2Harness2 | R2App | start=harness, convo=mcp | `fxHarness` + `harness-lifecycle-mcp.json` (v2/harness/harness.test.tsx) | V2-T17 (Gateway MCP read, P16) | C32 |\n| R2Harness3 | R2App | start=harness, convo=keys | `fxHarness` + `harness-lifecycle-keys.json` (v2/harness/harness.test.tsx) | V2-T17, T18 | C32 |\n| R2Api | R2App | start=api | `fxApi` (v2/fixtures.ts; v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx) | V2-T14; V2-R05, T05 in `ui_v2_workbench` | C33 |\n| R2Cases | R2App | start=cases | `fxCases` (v2/fixtures.ts; v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx) | V2-T15, T16 | C33 |\n| Show the calls | R2App, any start (no prototype board) | `fxCalls` (v2/fixtures.ts; v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx) | panel shown only while chosen, never a secret (P54) | C33 |\n| R2Academy | R2App | start=academy | `fx.academy` | embed mounts, theme | C34 |\n\nTest ids: `V2-Txx` Vitest (desktop app), `V2-Rxx` Rust integration\n(desktop-core), `V2-Nxx` native checks (`native-checks.json`). Registry of\nids: [../invariants.md](../invariants.md) plus the per-screen contracts.\n## D014 — Rust application authority\n\nAccepted in interview round 4, Q14.\n\nRust owns tenant context, credential access, request lifecycles, and permission\nto apply configuration changes. React presents drafts, reviews, and results.\nConfiguration review binds the tenant, credentials, resource, and draft; changed\ncontext invalidates it. Harness proposals enter the same operator review flow\nand cannot authorize Apply. Initially preserve the existing Harness project/tool\nrestrictions; expansion would require a separate explicit design decision.\n\n## D015 — Import work, reestablish authentication\n\nAccepted in interview round 4, Q15.\n\nImport selected user-authored work and settings, including saved cases, reports,\nAcademy drafts, API Client projects, and historical conversations. Require fresh\ncredential setup and sign-in. Regenerate disposable caches/downloads. Imported\nconversations are inspectable history until resumption compatibility is validated;\nold pending approvals and authentication sessions never transfer.\n\nReading protected source work for an explicitly selected import is distinct from\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
