ditional key… reviewed and confirmed natively, the issued key revealed through the host's secret sheet, the review exit, the Inbox reminder and its resumption, the old key's removal (invariants I6/I7) | C31-N03 pass |\ndocs/planning/evidence/C44/legacy-script-map.md-338-| C31-N04 | The accessibility additions (DESIGN-V2 §8) on the changed UI: the review sheet is the one topmost modal (the rail hidden beneath it) and Escape closes it with focus re… | exercised | C39-N02 — the review sheet docked with Close review and Done | C39-N02 pass |\ndocs/planning/evidence/C44/legacy-script-map.md-339-| C32-N01 | The Harness renders in the v2 shell on the existing engine: the title row names the tenant, the engine and the workspace; the prerequisites checklist is hidden once sa… | exercised | C38-N01 — the title band names tenant, engine and workspace; a fresh tenant's first send starts a conversation | C38-N01 pass |\ndocs/planning/evidence/C44/legacy-script-map.md-340-| C32-N02 | A command the engine asks to run while the project is read-only is decided in the page (Approve once / Decline) after a project is chosen through the embedded project … | exercised | C38-N01, C38-N02, C38-N03 — a decision held in the aside; Approve once / Decline; a tenant switch while it waits meets the guard | C38-N01 pass, C38-N02 pass, C38-N03 pass |\ndocs/planning/evidence/C44/legacy-script-map.md-341-| C32-N03 | The workspace MCP catalog read the engine asks for (airs_desktop.mcpServers) is shown as read-only and read only once approved in the page; a change the engine propose… | exercised | C38-N01 — the mcpServers read waits, is approved in the page and made once | C38-N01 pass |\ndocs/planning/evidence/C44/legacy-script-map.md-342-| C32-N04 | Keyboard: Tab from the message box reaches Send or End; at the 900×600 minimum and 200% zoom in both themes nothing on the Harness screen lies past the window's right … | exercised | C38-N02 — Tab from the message box; 900×600 at 200% without horizontal scroll | C38-N02 pass |\n# C44 — retired legacy native assertions (for the owner's acceptance)\n\nEvery pre-P09 native assertion the one presentation does not exercise natively is listed here with its reason (`tools/native-acceptance/legacy_assertions.py`, kind `r`). The gate (`acceptance_c44.py`, C44-N01) accepts a retirement only when its id is listed in this file and the acceptance line below is present; an assertion removed from this file must gain a native target or the gate fails.\n\nNot retired: the tenant-switch guard with a Harness decision pending (C30-N01, invariant I1) is exercised natively on the Harness board (C38-N03: the switcher, the palette and the Go menu; Stay; Archive and switch), and the staged Runtime key rotation with the host's reveal (C31-N03, invariants I6/I7) by acceptance_c31.py running on the one presentation.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nAccepted by the owner on 2026-10-31. Asked whether to accept the 90 retirements listed below (11 under D060, 6 under D059, 73 whose behaviour the named core or renderer suites hold with no native driver on the one presentation) or to port some into native drivers first, the owner answered, in their own words: \"accepted\". Every retirement below stands on that acceptance; a change to this list is a new decision. Of the 90 accepted, C30-N01 and C31-N03 were then exercised natively after all (C38-N03 on the Harness board; acceptance_c31.py on the one presentation) and stand as exercised in the map, not retired; 88 remain retired.\n\n## D060 — no import from the alpha (11)\n\n| Legacy check | What it asserted | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| C02-N06 | Profile import through the native open sheet attached to the main window: a synthetic airs-cli registry with an embedded synthetic secret an… | the airs-cli profile import is retired by D060 (no import from the alpha; its removal is the follow-up chunk's) |\n| C23-N01 | Import from v1 is available in the shell. Look for v1 data finds the staged fixture v1 folder without