eview, item checkboxes, Import, Import again aft… | retired by D060 (no import from the alpha): the destination, view, wizard links and first-run frame are removed; no replacement |\n| C23-N09 | Lost import records fail closed and are said: with a receipt damaged in both of its files the import view names it in an alert, Remove damag… | retired by D060 (no import from the alpha): the destination, view, wizard links and first-run frame are removed; no replacement |\n| C14-N13 | Profile adoption previews the staged v1 API Client profile, imports the selected collection into Recent with its private environment, never … | profile adoption from the alpha is retired by D060 (its removal is the follow-up chunk's) |\n\n## D059 — the prototype has no such surface (the legacy shell, or a view it does not draw) (6)\n\n| Legacy check | What it asserted | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| C13-N02 | Choosing another statistics window reads that window (LAST_7_DAYS) and says which window is shown.… | the statistics window choice is not on the prototype's card (D059); the windowed read is the core's: crates/desktop-core/tests/redteam_model_reads |\n| C18-N02 | One run is sent only when Run is pressed: once, with the inference key (no management authorization) to the stored endpoint, streaming, at m… | the Gateway Playground is not on the prototype's Gateway card (D059: Overview, Workspaces, Routes, Providers, Guardrails, Keys, Integrations, Logs, MCP servers); inference is exercised through the Harness (C38-N01) and the core's crates/desktop-core/tests/gateway_inference |\n| C18-N03 | Stop ends a run mid-stream: the stream is closed, the response says the Gateway may have run and charged for it, and the run is kept on this… | stopping a Gateway Playground run: crates/desktop-core/tests/gateway_inference (no Gateway Playground on the one presentation, D059) |\n| C18-N10 | Run prompt is keyboard-reachable at 200% zoom and Remove key at the minimum window size, inside the window; a chart's v